{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038","id":"pg_71891dfc5c5c5214877bcac3f576b141","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sinameraji-kimiflare-plan-md-efe84a2e65dc-cac3f576b141.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9e1dd4a2c9695dcf8bcb38750299ac8d"],"title":"sinameraji/kimiflare/PLAN.md @ efe84a2e65dc","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3d14e3506855e00df38745874bb293139acd35244e80b9d9cd799a9989e41e92"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In Camouflage UI mode, every inbound event is persisted to a SQLite WAL database (~/.config/kimiflare/camouflage-sessions.db), making sessions replayable via a --replay flag."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cea5a85715c07cf110ae0802d469ae9def4b93a50072fecbff71061f0a73329d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The experimental Camouflage renderer is an external package (camouflage-tui, e.g. 2.1.0-beta.1 as an optionalDependency) whose upstream capabilities gate some features like renderer-side mouse events."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3d14e3506855e00df38745874bb293139acd35244e80b9d9cd799a9989e41e92","clm_cea5a85715c07cf110ae0802d469ae9def4b93a50072fecbff71061f0a73329d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038","id":"pg_7bc79bf676b1543cbde8a969dcec4c1a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sinameraji-kimiflare-camouflage-migration-md-efe84a2e65dc-a969dcec4c1a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ce204fca4bac564f9617609bffd201db"],"title":"sinameraji/kimiflare/CAMOUFLAGE_MIGRATION.md @ efe84a2e65dc","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1e20bc3a0b273bd7210aaf6f7b0403fe91970a482a0f70ddd8ce043006ea3741"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An incident report documents that v0.29.0's multi-agent mode broke legacy /resume context, omitted system prompts for built-in agents, and crashed auto-compact; a fix was implemented but pending merge at report time."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d9b8792bee3ab4db4dc5b5adf94a8cd63853fa1d4d88b126ae3fad6ab5dc2595"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A multi-agent feature (PR #220, v0.29.0) uses an AgentOrchestrator with per-agent message buffers and built-in research/coding/generalist agents."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1e20bc3a0b273bd7210aaf6f7b0403fe91970a482a0f70ddd8ce043006ea3741","clm_d9b8792bee3ab4db4dc5b5adf94a8cd63853fa1d4d88b126ae3fad6ab5dc2595"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038","id":"pg_91019a25769c59e68517a4889a007e1d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sinameraji-kimiflare-incident-report-2026-05-01-multi-agent-resume-reg-a4889a007e1d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9fd5d62550a557be90bb5d68eeb49ce8"],"title":"sinameraji/kimiflare/incident-report-2026-05-01-multi-agent-resume-regression.md @ efe84a2e65dc","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_07d62dc45074a543013b1918656f828a91c0770cd34ec093d73cb8f3564a1c58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint can replace all Cloudflare paths via KIMIFLARE_BASE_URL/KIMIFLARE_API_KEY or config.json baseUrl/apiKey, making Cloudflare credentials optional."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e2b0b10cb7ef6a90713d5daee8c342d5ee2d4a19631338f9a67c684b5422cbc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three permission modes exist: plan (read-only tools only, blocking writes, mutating bash, MCP, and LSP renames), edit (default, prompts per mutating call), and auto (approves everything)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_26438b7217de2457ef070ac80436b1d3bdec8b6addf04bd206dc5b0b30ee5724"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The default model is @cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code with 262k context, reasoning, tools, and vision; kimi-k2.6, kimi-k2.5, and @cf/zai-org/glm-5.2 are also available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3d4c28a2cdbc936efb309d08cd1cfb41ed66a1d4f7eeb93d63314c5628e939de"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool requires Node.js >= 20 and is distributed via npm (installable globally or run with npx)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_576bf082e937c9eb4c3190084c51dd6d379d895a2f4a4805aead5b0986865d46"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent-side activity logs are written as daily JSONL files under ~/.config/kimiflare/logs with 7-day retention pruned at startup; prompts and completions are deliberately excluded, with Gateway request_id for joining."},{"claim_ids":["clm_627d10ad186d70aa5f8375151a2179d6cb7fe88605b62c94c0b8912107f4c91f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"One-shot CLI usage supports -p prompts, --dangerously-allow-all for auto-approving mutating tools in scripts, and --reasoning to include chain-of-thought on stderr."},{"claim_ids":["clm_76ad319cdbe2a0ddfdba07295c4293a9d9aeba398c5ab8445d331ebb0ce8783e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A JSONL-over-stdio RPC mode (--mode rpc) supports new_session, prompt, resolve_permission, and session resume for non-Node or isolated consumers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_820eecef5bb29c1eb29da45ae89a3ac435cd2eb3c000d12a5c4944b2d5c236b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors fork, branch, run npm run typecheck and npm run build, commit with Conventional Commits, and open a PR; scripts include tsup build, tsx dev, and npm test."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8c86acb7472e7b6e1c49d2ca389b6ffd69d5c739c1e4e9d3d02f86a0ef7dd934"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"KimiFlare is a terminal coding agent powered by Kimi K2.7 on Cloudflare Workers AI, running entirely on the user's own Cloudflare account, with optional AI Gateway routing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_98dc5828badc693b40697232184c9c8c410d7fddcaa784b928f9ef072c61481d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Slash commands include /mode, /shell, /thinking, /theme, /resume, /compact, /init, /memory, /mcp, /cost, /gateway status, /update, and /help."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a66e8f031201e015b07633a1f7f76dc065cc41a0c9cb1db12459ea134c5fc762"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A headless SDK exposes createAgentSession with subscribe/prompt/steer/followUp/pause/resume/getStatus/getUsage, typed events, a custom permissionHandler, and optional memoryEnabled/lspEnabled/costAttribution flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d58328533dd38191c4459baa40904ff2bb3244c4dc8c9d046cda1c237bdc637c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hooks fire shell commands at five turn points (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, UserPromptSubmit, Stop, PreCompact); non-zero exit on veto events cancels the action, with matcher regex, timeoutMs (default 30000), and enable/disable support."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dac6ff2d1ec44e8fc8a5594879e809f85356e2e6b0c0458088abdb226ad37cd2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Log entries can be shipped to an OpenTelemetry collector via KIMIFLARE_OTEL_ENDPOINT over OTLP/HTTP, batched every 5s or 100 entries, best-effort so the agent loop is never blocked."}],"claim_ids":["clm_07d62dc45074a543013b1918656f828a91c0770cd34ec093d73cb8f3564a1c58","clm_0e2b0b10cb7ef6a90713d5daee8c342d5ee2d4a19631338f9a67c684b5422cbc","clm_26438b7217de2457ef070ac80436b1d3bdec8b6addf04bd206dc5b0b30ee5724","clm_3d4c28a2cdbc936efb309d08cd1cfb41ed66a1d4f7eeb93d63314c5628e939de","clm_576bf082e937c9eb4c3190084c51dd6d379d895a2f4a4805aead5b0986865d46","clm_627d10ad186d70aa5f8375151a2179d6cb7fe88605b62c94c0b8912107f4c91f","clm_76ad319cdbe2a0ddfdba07295c4293a9d9aeba398c5ab8445d331ebb0ce8783e","clm_820eecef5bb29c1eb29da45ae89a3ac435cd2eb3c000d12a5c4944b2d5c236b9","clm_8c86acb7472e7b6e1c49d2ca389b6ffd69d5c739c1e4e9d3d02f86a0ef7dd934","clm_98dc5828badc693b40697232184c9c8c410d7fddcaa784b928f9ef072c61481d","clm_a66e8f031201e015b07633a1f7f76dc065cc41a0c9cb1db12459ea134c5fc762","clm_d58328533dd38191c4459baa40904ff2bb3244c4dc8c9d046cda1c237bdc637c","clm_dac6ff2d1ec44e8fc8a5594879e809f85356e2e6b0c0458088abdb226ad37cd2"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038","id":"pg_bbbf3cdaca2c57be9792d8bf31f76939","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sinameraji-kimiflare-readme-md-efe84a2e65dc-d8bf31f76939.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a5d39445c3335202af8a4235edbd6a05"],"title":"sinameraji/kimiflare/README.md @ efe84a2e65dc","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3beaa88b79544644b05b46da4a2f5038"}
